[1;38;5;16;48;5;208m 1 [0m [1mlib/home_screen.dart:41:13[0m
    🔴 [38;5;81mshrinkwrap-in-column[0m [38;5;245m·[0m high impact [38;5;245m·[0m [38;5;221m💡 suggestion[0m
    shrinkWrap in a SingleChildScrollView builds every item at once: ListView.builder is no longer lazy.
    If it scrolls together with other content: use CustomScrollView(slivers: [..., SliverList.builder(...)]),
    with SliverToBoxAdapter for the other widgets, and remove shrinkWrap.

[1;38;5;16;48;5;208m 2 [0m [1mlib/main.dart:10:3[0m
    ⚪ [38;5;81mserial-awaits-main[0m [38;5;245m·[0m low impact [38;5;245m·[0m [38;5;221m💡 suggestion[0m
    2 awaits run one after another before runApp, so the first frame waits for each in turn.
    If none of them needs another, start them together:
      final (_, catalog) = await (
        SystemChrome.setPreferredOrientations([DeviceOrientation.portraitUp]),
        rootBundle.loadString('assets/catalog.json'),
      ).wait;
    Keep any call that must finish first (like Firebase.initializeApp before other Firebase calls) above it.
    If one fails, .wait throws a ParallelWaitError (the original error is inside it), so a catch on a specific exception type stops matching. Keep them separate if you catch errors here.

[1;38;5;16;48;5;208m 3 [0m [1mlib/product_tile.dart:15:14[0m
    ⚪ [38;5;81mintrinsic-in-list[0m [38;5;245m·[0m low impact [38;5;245m·[0m [38;5;221m💡 suggestion[0m
    IntrinsicHeight lays out its child twice for every list item that is built.
    If the items can have a known height, SizedBox(height: ...) skips the extra pass.
    If the height depends on the content, keeping it is fine in a lazy list: only visible items pay.

